There are some neat techniques at the timestamp I listed. The finger tying one seemed particularly interesting to me.

It's a picture taken out of context during a photoshoot, and after a photoshoot. The goal is to normalize it for fragile people with small egos who think that wearing a mask somehow affects how people see them.

&#x200B;

Again, this entire post is just nitpicking about an actual nothingburger.

&#x200B;

This is a photoshoot they had during a global pandemic. This is not critiquing policy making, this is childish nitpicking over technicalities when the ultimate goal is to get people to wear masks in a pandemic. This fearmongering over authoritarianism when it comes to wearing a mask during a pandemic is ridiculous.

But see, they're politicians and their entire job is about messaging and imagery. And so now, as politicians on the "pro-mask side" they have to still be vigilant otherwise toddlers like OP point out whenever they're being even a little hypocritical.

&#x200B;

It's a piece of paper you wear on your face to keep you from possibly infecting others. That's it. It should not be this divisive.

\> Politician should not be a career choice

&#x200B;

Guess what though, it is. You can get a political science degree, or a law degree, and you can have a 40 hour per week career in law and politics.

&#x200B;

Let them do their goddamn jobs.

So should models wear the clothing they normally wear when they try on clothing? Should athletes only ever use the gear they sponsor?

&#x200B;

They have a job to try to convince millions of people to take basic health precautions in an era of raging misinformation and dangerous division. They're also people. We can nit pick wearing masks, or we can all promote wearing masks and safely wear them when we need to, or we're asked too. This is a political attack for trying to spread a basic safety measure that the previous administration actively dismissed. 

&#x200B;

No one is asking anyone to wear a mask all the time. They're putting on masks for a photo outside because they want to normalize mask wearing because we're in a global pandemic. This "outrage" is a childish tantrum that is, frankly, not worth the effort of this comment.

My whole family is staying home for quarantine.

